<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shutruk-Nahhunte</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shutruk-Nahhunte was a king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elam">Elam</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shutrukid-dynasty">Shutrukid dynasty</a> in the twelfth century BCE. Together with his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kutir-nahhunte">Kutir-Nahhunte</a> he defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kassite-dynasty">Kassite dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a> around 1158 BCE. He carried off Mesopotamian monuments such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/code-of-hammurabi">Code of Hammurabi</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/susa">Susa</a> as war trophies.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shutruk-nahhunte.jpg" alt="Shutruk-Nahhunte" width="284" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Darafsh · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shutruk-Nakhunte,_Mus%C3%A9e_du_Louvre.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
